if {game_state} == 2.0:
	if {first_talk} == false:
		Seelie: Ooh come here come here Acacia! Looks like we have a new friend~
		set {first_talk} = true
		[signal arg="come here"]
	else:
		if {crow_intervened} == 0.0:
			Acacia: Oh! A new lost soul! A new plaything! Lucky us! Now what’s your name, pet?
			You: I can’t remember…
			Seelie: A clever one I see!
			Seelie: ~tricky trickyyyy~
			You: Huh?
			Acacia: Very clever one we have, Eulalia
			Acacia: Mortal, why don’t you join us in a dance?
			Seelie: Oh yes, clever mortal! You must, you must!!
			Seelie: Come! Come join us in our dance!
			You: That sounds like fun…
			You: but I really don’t have the time right now
			You: I’m looking for some… berries?
			Seelie: Oh Acacia, didn’t we find some berries right
			Acacia: here! Come mortal
			Acacia: we will give you the berries you seek and then you will join us in celebratory dance!
			Acacia: You must
			Seelie: You must join us and welcome the arrival of Spring properly!
			Seelie: Come now, mortal. What say you?
			You: That sounds goo—
			[signal arg="crow"]
			audio "res://audio/sound_effects/813114__qubodup__crow-call.ogg" [volume="-10.0"]
			set {crow_intervened} = 1.0
		elif {crow_intervened} == 1.0:
			Crow: Ladies, this little one is new here
			Crow: you wouldn’t be taking advantage of that, would you?
			Crow: Let me handle the negotiation
			The crow whispers to you
			Crow: Follow my lead if your soul is precious to you
			You: Uh, oka—
			Crow: I found this beautiful ribbon earlier today when scavenging to build my nest
			Crow: It is quite pleasing to the eyes and would make a beautiful hair accessory
			Crow: I can offer it as yours in exchange for the berries
			Crow: Do we have a deal?
			Acacia: Hmm… I much prefer the dancing deal we were about to make with our new plaything before you got involved to spoil our fun…
			Seelie: Oh, what a beautiful silken shining thing it is!
			Seelie: Yes, this will look beautiful in my hair!
			Seelie: Acacia, if you could braid/plait it into my hair for me…
			Seelie: Oh! All the others of the Spring Court will be so envious at the ball!
			Seelie: Yes, this deal pleases me greatly, Crow!
			Crow: Perfect! So we have a fair deal then?
			The crow gave the Seelie duo the shiny ribbon in exchange for the berries
			Crow: Now please excuse me and my little friend here
			Crow: They promised to help me with my nest, isn’t that right?
			You: Uh… did I?
			Crow: Ahem
			You: Oh, yes absolutely
			set {game_state} = 3.0
			[signal arg="crow takes berries"]
elif {game_state} >= 3.0:
	if {game_state} < 7.0:
		Seelie: Please dance with us, mortal
	elif {game_state} >= 7.0 and {game_state} < 8.0:
		elif {seelie_invited} == 0.0:
			Seelie: Clever mortal! Were you truly not going to tell us? Were you?
			You: Apologies, but tell you what?
			Acacia: The dance! The dance, mortal
			Acacia: You were not planning on dancing without us certainly?
			You: The dance?
			You: Oh! Well, it’s not really a dance
			You: I’m going to be playing a tune to awaken the crocus of spring and—
			Seelie: Yes, yes, so a dance then
			Seelie: You would not forget us in this, would you, mortal?
			Acacia: You did promise us a dance
			Acacia: You would not forget such promises now, would you, pet?
			You: I don’t recall making any such promises to dance with you, but of course, I don’t mean to offend
			You: I will be performing with a fiddle, but please come, both of you
			You: I will enjoy watching your dancing
			Seelie: As we will surely enjoy your tune
			Seelie: Oh, this is so exciting Acacia! A new song, isn’t it wonderful?
			Acacia: Certainly, Eulalia
			Acacia: I still wish our little pet would take up the dance with us
			Acacia: but a fine melody will very much suffice
			You: I will be performing it soon!
			You: If you both head toward the first flower of spring
			You: I will be there shortly to start the performance
			Acacia: Wonderful indeed, pet
			Acacia: I hope it is not a performance to disappoint
			Acacia: Bringing revelry is certainly always a more pleasing outcome than sowing disappointment, you know
			You: I will be doing my best
			You: I mean, no matter what else, I must if I want spring to awaken
			Seelie: Pay Acacia no mind, clever mortal
			Seelie: She is just hungry for a new fascination and not so high in patience
			Seelie: I am sure your performance will not disappoint us
			Seelie: Goodbye goodbye for now
			Acacia: We will be seeing you soon, pet
			set {seelie_invited} = 1.0
		elif {seelie_invited} == 1.0:
			Acacia: We will be seeing you soon, pet
	elif {game_state} == 8.0:
		Acacia: What a wonderful tune mortal
		Acacia: Surely it would have left your body wanting to move
		Acacia: Why don't you join me for a nice waltz
		Acacia: The old goat could give us a rythm
		Seelie: Oh Acacia, you're ruining the atmosphere with your obsession
		Seelie: Clever mortal, that was a wonderful performance indeed